          <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg border-2 border-gray-100 hover:border-primary/20 transition-all" data-aos="fade-up-sm" data-aos-delay="100">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">How is professional tile cleaning different from mopping?</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
              Mopping just moves dirty water around the surface and pushes grime into your grout. Professional tile cleaning uses rotary equipment and powerful extraction to remove dirt from deep within porous grout lines—something a mop simply can't do.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg border-2 border-gray-100 hover:border-primary/20 transition-all" data-aos="fade-up-sm" data-aos-delay="150">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">What types of tile can you clean?</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
              We clean all types of tile, including ceramic, porcelain, travertine, slate, marble, and other natural stone. Each surface requires specialized care, and our technicians are trained to handle them all safely and effectively.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg border-2 border-gray-100 hover:border-primary/20 transition-all" data-aos="fade-up-sm" data-aos-delay="200">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">Should I seal my grout?</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
              Absolutely. Unsealed grout is porous and absorbs everything—dirt, spills, bacteria. Sealing creates a waterproof barrier that prevents stains, makes cleaning easier, and extends the life of your grout. We highly recommend it after every deep cleaning.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg border-2 border-gray-100 hover:border-primary/20 transition-all" data-aos="fade-up-sm" data-aos-delay="250">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">How long does grout sealing last?</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
              With proper care, professionally sealed grout can last 3-5 years or longer. High-traffic areas may need resealing sooner. We'll inspect your grout during our service and let you know if resealing is necessary.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg border-2 border-gray-100 hover:border-primary/20 transition-all" data-aos="fade-up-sm" data-aos-delay="300">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">Can you remove stains from grout?</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
              In most cases, yes. Our professional cleaning process removes years of built-up dirt and stains, restoring grout to its original color. However, if grout has been permanently dyed by certain substances, we may recommend color sealing as an alternative.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg border-2 border-gray-100 hover:border-primary/20 transition-all" data-aos="fade-up-sm" data-aos-delay="350">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">How long does the cleaning take?</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
              It depends on the size of the area and the level of soiling. Most tile and grout cleaning jobs take 2-4 hours. If you add grout sealing, allow additional time for the sealant to cure. We'll provide a time estimate during your free consultation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg border-2 border-gray-100 hover:border-primary/20 transition-all" data-aos="fade-up-sm" data-aos-delay="400">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">When can I walk on the floors after cleaning?</h3>
            <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
              Your tile floors are safe to walk on immediately after cleaning. If you opt for grout sealing, we recommend staying off the sealed areas for 2-4 hours to allow the sealant to cure properly. We'll provide specific care instructions based on your service.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg border-2 border-gray-100 hover:border-primary/20 transition-all" data-aos="fade-up-sm" data-aos-delay="450">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">Do you offer a satisfaction guarantee?</h3>
